    "show_share": true,
    "description": "AKU-IED's recent Kazim Bacchus Research Seminar featured a thought-provoking presentation by Dr Saulat Pervez, a researcher from the International Institute of Islamic Thought (IIIT) in Virginia, USA. The seminar, titled 'Locating Pakistani Mid-Tier Private Schools in Local & Global Educational Discourses,' provided an in-depth analysis based on Dr Pervez's extensive research and experiences in Pakistan and other parts of the world. Dr Pervez, with her vast experience in Karachi's private schooling sector, explored the complexities of postcolonial cultures influencing social class, language disparities, and reading attitudes. She delved into the challenges posed by the dominance of English, which marginalizes the native language, Urdu, and hampers the development of reading and writing cultures in both languages. Her research is particularly focused on bi/multilingual contexts and how these dynamics affect educational outcomes.",
